  "title": "Trimmer potentiometer, 1/4 inch square (3362P)",
  "summary": "Single-turn cermet trimmer you set once with a screwdriver, such as a comparator's threshold. Its three pins sit in a triangle on the breadboard grid. Seen from the top with the printed face toward you, `a` is the left pin, `b` the right and `wiper` the one behind them. Turning clockwise moves the wiper from `a` toward `b`. Set its resistance, the value printed on top (103 is 10k). `position` is the wiper's place along the track, the share of `resistance` between `a` and `wiper`, above 0 and below 1. The buy link is the 10 kΩ value of the series.",
